    "anchor": "PBPS2609.06905v1 Section2.2 equations2.6-2.14 and AppendixC.1 omitted same-solution compact localization analytic prerequisite; SPHMC2609.06906v1 Section4.1 actual BL dependency only. No numbered source localization theorem is claimed.",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
    "original_text": "Explicit analytic prerequisite restatement:\nE is a finite-dimensional real Hilbert space with Borel measurable structure and canonical full-space volume, including dimension zero. W is C1, exp(-W) is integrable, and mu is exactly volume.tilted(-W).\nD is the original closable partial gradient on L2(mu), with graph exactly compact smooth scalar representatives and their genuine gradients modulo mu-a.e. D is fixed before epsilon>0 and forcing f in L2(mu). The genuine solution u/G/r and all local volume facts are derived, not supplied.\nFor every C2 real cutoff chi with compact topological support, the same u chosen before all chi yields explicit v=chi*u, Gchi=chi*G+u*grad chi and Fchi=chi*r+2 inner(grad chi,G)+u Delta chi. Neither sign, normalized mass, compact derivative bounds nor localized PDE/H2 certificate is assumed. All localized L2 and test integrals use volume; variational identities use L2(mu).\nFor the exact normalized Gibbs mu, original closable D fixed before epsilon/forcing, construct the actual resolvent u in D.closure.domain. Retain the actual all-domain variational equation, ordinary locally integrable u/G, all C1 compact directional weak-gradient tests, squared local integrability of r=epsilon*u+inner(grad W,G)-f, compact-volume L2 of u/G/r and every C2 original distribution test. For every C2 compact chi define v=chi*u, Gchi=chi*G+u*grad chi, Fchi=chi*r+2 inner(grad chi,G)+u Delta chi. Prove genuine global-volume L2 of v/Gchi/Fchi and each topological support contained in tsupport chi. For every C1 compact psi/direction a both weak-gradient products are L1 with integral psi inner(Gchi,a)=-integral v Dpsi[a]. For every C2 compact phi both PDE products are L1 with integral v Delta phi=integral Fchi phi. The same u is chosen before all cutoffs; only smooth test/cutoff functions have classical derivatives.\nSame actual original D/u/G/r, one u before all C2 compact chi: derive actual compact support/global volume L2 of chi*u, chi*G+u*gradchi, chi*r+2<gradchi,G>+u*Delta chi, all C1 compact weak-gradient and C2 compact distribution PDE with every L1 term legal. No localized weighted closure-domain membership, H2, Schwartz/tempered adapter, global core/Bochner, BL/Poincare, epsilon0, noncompact domain, measurable y-selector or either main/composition. Reflected/RGO law/scale remain distinct; TV never transfers unbounded expected cost.",
    "text_sha256": "ab6ef4d45b874656f14f99efabb55443dbb7b575f4c8fc063943545850a2dd6f"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.LocalizedWeakResolvent.localized_weak_resolvent",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/FunctionalInequalities/LocalizedWeakResolvent.lean",
    "statement": "(W : E → ℝ) (hW : ContDiff ℝ 1 W)\n    (hI : Integrable (fun x => Real.exp (-W x))) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -W x)\n    ∀ (D : Lp ℝ 2 μ →ₗ.[ℝ] Lp E 2 μ), D.IsClosable →\n      (∀ (a : Lp ℝ 2 μ) (H : Lp E 2 μ), (a,H) ∈ D.graph ↔\n        ∃ φ : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ ∞ φ ∧ HasCompactSupport φ ∧\n          a =ᵐ[μ] φ ∧ H =ᵐ[μ] gradient φ) →\n      ∀ (ε : ℝ), 0 < ε → ∀ f : Lp ℝ 2 μ,\n      ∃ u : D.closure.domain,\n        (∀ v : D.closure.domain,\n          ε * ⟪(u : Lp ℝ 2 μ), (v : Lp ℝ 2 μ)⟫ +\n            ⟪D.closure u, D.closure v⟫ = ⟪f, (v : Lp ℝ 2 μ)⟫) ∧\n        LocallyIntegrable (fun x => (u : Lp ℝ 2 μ) x) ∧\n        LocallyIntegrable (fun x => D.closure u x) ∧\n        (∀ ψ : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ 1 ψ → HasCompactSupport ψ → ∀ v : E,\n          Integrable (fun x => ψ x * inner ℝ (D.closure u x) v) ∧\n          Integrable (fun x => (u : Lp ℝ 2 μ) x * fderiv ℝ ψ x v) ∧\n          (∫ x, ψ x * inner ℝ (D.closure u x) v) =\n            - ∫ x, (u : Lp ℝ 2 μ) x * fderiv ℝ ψ x v) ∧\n        LocallyIntegrable (fun x => ‖ε * (u : Lp ℝ 2 μ) x +\n          inner ℝ (gradient W x) (D.closure u x) - f x‖ ^ 2) ∧\n        (∀ K : Set E, IsCompact K →\n          MemLp (fun x => (u : Lp ℝ 2 μ) x) 2 (volume.restrict K) ∧\n          MemLp (fun x => D.closure u x) 2 (volume.restrict K) ∧\n          MemLp (fun x => ε * (u : Lp ℝ 2 μ) x +\n            inner ℝ (gradient W x) (D.closure u x) - f x) 2 (volume.restrict K)) ∧\n        (∀ φ : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ 2 φ → HasCompactSupport φ →\n          Integrable (fun x => (u : Lp ℝ 2 μ) x * Laplacian.laplacian φ x) ∧\n          Integrable (fun x => (ε * (u : Lp ℝ 2 μ) x +\n            inner ℝ (gradient W x) (D.closure u x) - f x) * φ x) ∧\n          (∫ x, (u : Lp ℝ 2 μ) x * Laplacian.laplacian φ x) =\n            ∫ x, (ε * (u : Lp ℝ 2 μ) x +\n              inner ℝ (gradient W x) (D.closure u x) - f x) * φ x) ∧\n        ∀ χ : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ 2 χ → HasCompactSupport χ →\n    let v := fun x => χ x * (u : Lp ℝ 2 μ) x\n    let Gχ := fun x => χ x • D.closure u x + (u : Lp ℝ 2 μ) x • gradient χ x\n    let Fχ := fun x => χ x * (ε * (u : Lp ℝ 2 μ) x + inner ℝ (gradient W x) (D.closure u x) - f x) + 2 * inner ℝ (gradient χ x) (D.closure u x) +\n      (u : Lp ℝ 2 μ) x * Laplacian.laplacian χ x\n    MemLp v 2 volume ∧ MemLp Gχ 2 volume ∧ MemLp Fχ 2 volume ∧\n    tsupport v ⊆ tsupport χ ∧ tsupport Gχ ⊆ tsupport χ ∧ tsupport Fχ ⊆ tsupport χ ∧\n    (∀ ψ : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ 1 ψ → HasCompactSupport ψ → ∀ a : E,\n      Integrable (fun x => ψ x * inner ℝ (Gχ x) a) ∧\n      Integrable (fun x => v x * fderiv ℝ ψ x a) ∧\n      (∫ x, ψ x * inner ℝ (Gχ x) a) = -∫ x, v x * fderiv ℝ ψ x a) ∧\n    ∀ φ : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ 2 φ → HasCompactSupport φ →\n      Integrable (fun x => v x * Laplacian.laplacian φ x) ∧\n      Integrable (fun x => Fχ x * φ x) ∧\n      (∫ x, v x * Laplacian.laplacian φ x) = ∫ x, Fχ x * φ x",
    "statement_sha256": "e531ef43ac0d965f9e4d49ca859dbf4c90b44fe414a6db3fa56ae1f32ffd13d6",
